            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Eli Whitney's Early Life</strong><br>\nEli Whitney was born in 1765 in Westborough, Massachusetts. He showed an early aptitude for mechanical work and invention, leading him to graduate from Yale College in 1792, intending to become a lawyer.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Cotton Gin Invention</strong><br>\nAfter observing the laborious process of cleaning cotton, Whitney invented the cotton gin in 1793, a machine that quickly and efficiently removed the seeds from cotton fibers. This invention revolutionized the cotton industry.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on the American South</strong><br>\nThe cotton gin vastly increased the production of cotton in the United States, particularly in the South, which became a cotton-rich region. This contributed to the entrenchment of slavery as plantation owners demanded more labor to grow cotton.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Manufacturing of Firearms</strong><br>\nWhitney is also known for his role in manufacturing firearms with interchangeable parts for the U.S. government. His methods contributed to the foundation of modern mass production and the American system of manufacturing.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legal Struggles Over Patents</strong><br>\nDespite the cotton gin's success, Whitney faced significant legal battles to protect his patent rights. The infringement of his invention by others left him with much less profit than the invention's impact would suggest.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Economic Contributions</strong><br>\nWhitney's innovations had a profound effect on the economy, facilitating the wide-scale processing of cotton in the United States and setting the stage for the Industrial Revolution through his work in the arms industry.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
